#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Benchmark the HSTU forward on production cross-attention cases.

    bench_hstu_prod_cases.py [--build BUILD] [--set igr_lsr_real|synthetic|all]
                             [--max-hints prod|real] [--verify] [--csv-out FILE] [--dry-run]

Runs tile_example_hstu_attention_fwd once per case with -perf=1 and prints each case's time and
TFLOPS plus per-set totals. All cases are fp16, jagged, cross-attention, softmax, non-causal,
nhead 1, hdim 128, inference (-training=0), with real per-sequence Q/KV lengths:

- igr_lsr_real: 100 calls of an IG Reels LSR model recorded in serving on MI350X, picked at
  evenly spaced quantiles of per-call sum(q * kv). The model passes max_seqlen = the batch's
  Q max and max_seqlen_kv = 40000 (a fixed cap); --max-hints real uses the batch's real maxima.
- synthetic: 4 shapes with production batch sizes and total Q/KV token counts (and, for two,
  the production max lengths and alpha); the per-sequence lengths are synthesized from the
  totals (seeded random split, capped at the max length where one is given).

K and V are separate tensors, as the example allocates them.
"""

